## The idea I want you to carry forward

There is a common thread connecting nearly everything in this module.

- Prefix sums remember cumulative information.
- Historical minimums remember the best previous candidate.
- Kadane's Algorithm remembers the best subarray ending at the current position.
- Prefix/suffix techniques remember information from both directions.
- Sliding windows remember the contents and properties of a current range.

The deeper lesson is learning what information an algorithm needs to remember, and what information it can safely discard.

That is one of the central skills behind algorithm design.

And that is precisely what we want to develop as you progress through DSA. 🚀